<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ilum-ma-ili</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ilum-ma-ili was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sealand-dynasty">Sealand Dynasty</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. After defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samsu-iluna">Samsu-iluna</a>, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a>, he broke the south away from Babylonian control. The Sealand's secession was a major territorial loss in the decline of the Babylonian Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ilum-ma-ili.jpg" alt="Ilum-ma-ili" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Gilgamesh_Dream_tablet._From_Iraq._Middle_Babylonian_Period,_First_Sealand_Dynasty,_1732-1460_BCE._Iraq_Museum,_Baghdad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
